  <p>
    To find the length of a curve <m>\vec{r}(t)</m> (its
    <m>\operatorname{arc}</m> length) on the interval <m>[a, b]</m>, we use
    a similar idea:
  </p>

  <p>
    Partition the curve into line segments, and add the length of each line
    segment to approximate the length of <m>\vec{r}(t)</m>.
  </p>

